---
import GenericPageLayout from '../../layouts/GenericPageLayout.astro';
import styles from '../../styles/about.module.css';
---

<GenericPageLayout 
  title="e-Library Portal" 
  subtitle="Access global scientific databases from anywhere on campus."
  heroImage="/media/DSC_4897.webp"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Library', href: '/library' },
    { label: 'e-Library', href: '/library/eportal' }
  ]}
>
  <div class={styles.contentWrapper}>
    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Seamless Digital Access</h2>
    <p class={styles.paragraph}>
      The e-Library portal provides authenticated access to premium, subscription-based agricultural, scientific, and engineering databases. These resources are strictly IP-restricted; you must be connected to the campus <strong>Eduroam Wi-Fi</strong> network or logged in via the institutional VPN to access full-text downloads.
    </p>

    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Subscribed Databases</h2>
    <ul class={styles.list}>
      <li><strong>JSTOR:</strong> Access to archived academic journals, primary sources, and books.</li>
      <li><strong>AGORA (Research4Life):</strong> Access to global research in agriculture, environmental science, and related biological sciences.</li>
      <li><strong>African Journals OnLine (AJOL):</strong> The world's largest online collection of African-published, peer-reviewed journals.</li>
      <li><strong>ProQuest Agricultural Science Collection:</strong> Comprehensive coverage of agricultural research and veterinary science literature.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class={styles.importantBox}>
      <strong>Remote VPN Access:</strong> If you are a student currently off-campus conducting fieldwork, you can request remote OpenVPN access from the Directorate of ICT to utilize the e-Library databases.
    </div>
  </div>
</GenericPageLayout>
